# Copy to .env (git-ignored). Never paste a key into chat or commit it; create it in the Anthropic Console and put it
# ONLY here (local) or in the Render dashboard → Environment (hosted). A user-scoped key (sk-ant-usr-…) also needs the
# workspace id (Console → Settings → Workspaces). The offline jury image never reads any of this.
# No access to the dashboard? Leave both empty: the UI's «Ключ Anthropic» field sends your key with each request
# (browser storage only, request header only, never stored on the server) — docs/AI_MODE.md «Bring your own key».

# --- Claude: the AI cross-check (/api/v1/verify, /api/v1/conflicts/scan) and the runtime AI path (?ai=…)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
# on a machine signed in with `ant auth login` instead of a key:
# JANA_AI_ASSUME_CREDENTIALS=1

# --- runtime AI path (docs/AI_MODE.md): off | foreign | fallback | always; the model and its effort
JANA_AI_MODE=off
JANA_AI_MODEL=claude-fable-5-1
JANA_AI_EFFORT=low

# --- a local vLLM / OpenAI-compatible labeler instead of Claude (university GPU): provider=openai-compatible
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=none

# local AI stack: docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.ai.yml up --build
